# Line endings are content in this repository, not formatting.
#
# `src/plugin/seed.rs` embeds `plugins/*.toml` with `include_str!`, and
# the upgrade path recognises an installed manifest by its sha256 — the same
# way `src/plugin/registry.rs` recognises a downloaded one. Git converts LF to
# CRLF on checkout by default on Windows, which changes those bytes: the same
# source then produces a different hash on a different machine, so a Windows
# build ships a built-in manifest whose declared hash does not describe it, and
# the migration that replaces the previous built-in never recognises what it is
# looking at. CI on windows-latest found exactly that.
#
# Checking every text file out with LF everywhere keeps "the manifest" one
# sequence of bytes, whoever built it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Screenshots and icons are bytes already; say so rather than leaving it to
# content sniffing.
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
